  "authoringDirection": "Build complete original pier footprint, northern stone retained causeway, southern discrete supported open bridge and native triangular/curved enlarged stone head with low corner turrets/side stairs. Do not fill all open sea section with a solid wall. Photographic pavilion: native octagonal two-storey plan, white open lower colonnade around red/dark inner body, red upper lattice windows, original teal/blue/gold geometric bracket bands, two genuinely curved orange-glazed tiled roofs with upswept corners/ridge tips and finial/lightning rod. Nativeroofprojections retained; symbolic5/10mheight tags not treated as survey. Blue handrails and six-lantern bronze-scroll white-pole rows along approach. Use single accepted modern original already inspected; hiddenpiers/lamps/detail/levels medium-fi approximations, no new broad sourcing needed. Whole natural sea/shore, nearby lighthouse/museum/city, visitors, logos, signs, paintings and temporaryrepairworks excluded. Preserve native geometry rather than force nominal440m.",
